From ef9e03c1d1784d60bbac28a4f84c87ce4301e0a9
Subject: bevy_gltf: pluggable resolver for the uris a glTF references
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/ef9e03c1d1784d60bbac28a4f84c87ce4301e0a9
Date: 2026-09-14T14:00:32+01:00

`load_image`, `texture_handle` and `load_buffers` joined every external
image/buffer uri onto the glTF's parent directory with `Path::join`, so a
uri with `..` segments never resolved and shared-texture layouts failed to
load. `GltfLoader::uri_resolver` (set via `GltfPlugin::with_uri_resolver`)
lets the host resolve those uris itself; `None` keeps the old join exactly.

`texture_handle` is the path the material's handle actually comes from for
external files, so the resolver is threaded through `load_material` and
the KHR_materials_* extensions as well as `load_image`.
---
